<!--
  Nicegram VR — the headset module's own strings.

  They live here rather than in Telegram's own strings.xml because upstream's file is
  synchronised from their cloud and anything of ours added to it is overwritten sooner or later.

  English only, on purpose, and translations do NOT belong beside this file. The package strips
  every Android locale (`localeFilters += ["zz"]`, TMessagesProj_AppQuest/build.gradle:124)
  because Telegram serves its own language packs at runtime, so a `values-ru/` here is compiled,
  merged, and then dropped from the APK — measured on the debug build of 2026-09-19, where
  `aapt2 dump resources` showed one `()` config per string and no locale config at all.

  The channel that works: read every one of these through `LocaleController.getString(res)`,
  which asks the language pack by this file's resource entry name and falls back to the English
  below. Russian is added by loading these keys into the pack, not by adding a folder here. The
  Russian source text that used to sit in `values-ru/strings_vr.xml` is in git history at
  7a54dbba and its successors.
-->
